        "body": "### Related\r\n\r\nCloses https://github.com/rerun-io/rerun/issues/10639\r\n\r\n### What\r\n\r\nThis PR switches us from collecting the entire dataset into memory to collecting a single partition into memory and then streaming out the results.  The remaining issues to address prior to merging are:\r\n\r\n- [x] ~~We're getting \"Data truncated due to size\" even when showing a tiny dataframe, just id and time. It should have many more rows.~~ This was a configuration issue\r\n- [x] I need to make sure I do some static queries also because they may break the time based portions\r\n- [x] Verify this works for ALL different time indices - time stamps vs i64 (u64?)\r\n- [x] Validate sorting is as expected - add unit tests\r\n- [x] Add tracing spans back in\r\n",
