          "patch_url": "https://github.com/rerun-io/rerun/pull/10123.patch",
          "merged_at": "2025-06-04T10:15:45Z"
        },
        "body": "### Related\r\n\r\n* #7484\r\n* Directly followed by https://github.com/rerun-io/rerun/pull/10125\r\n\r\n### What\r\n\r\nFirst PR in a series of PRs enabling \u2728 video streaming \u2728 \r\n\r\nChanges to how we capture the metadata of a video:\r\n* Introduce new `StableIndexDeque` and use it for everything in `re_video` that should support dropping & appending\r\n* `VideoData` -> `VideoDataDescription`\r\n* remove `re_video::Config`\r\n* make `StsdBox` optional on `VideoDataDescription` but add optional codec & `coded_dimensions` instead\r\n* duration of video samples and video as a whole is now optional (since video streams are open ended!)\r\n\r\nChanges to the video player (re_renderer):\r\n* allocate video frame texture lazily (we may not know the size ahead of time!)\r\n* `VideoChunkDecoder` -> `VideoSampleDecoder` for more consistent naming\r\n* video data description is no longer held via `Arc` but instead owned. This allows for editing it later on\r\n* handle some GC related cornercases to avoid out of bounds access notably still missing: be aware of dynamically growing GOPs",
